FullText:
A Mixed Method Study of Exploring the Phenomenon of Parentification in Chinese Families

Duties

The appointee will report to the Principal Investigator and be mainly responsible for the following core duties:

Assist in conducting research activities related to youth mental health and family process;
Assist in conducting interviews and focus group with participants;
Conduct qualitative analyses and statistical analyses;
Assist in writing research reports, academic papers, and other project‑related documents;
Liaise with NGOs for the logistic arrangement of data collection; and
Perform any other duties as assigned.
Requirements
A Bachelor’s degree in Journalism/Psychology/Sociology/Social Work or relevant social science disciplines;
Proficiency in speaking and understanding Cantonese and Putonghua;
Good writing skills in both English and Chinese;
Strong willingness to carry out field interviews; and
A strong sense of responsibility, initiative, and the ability to work both independently and in a team are required.
Preference will be given to candidates with research and work experience in social services.
Salary and Conditions of Service

Remuneration package will be highly competitive, commensurate with qualifications and experience.

Information and Application

Further information on the post and the University is available at http://www.cityu.edu.hk, or from the Human Resources Office, City University of Hong Kong, Tat Chee Avenue, Kowloon Tong, Hong Kong [Email : hrojob@cityu.edu.hk/Fax : 2788 1154 or 3442 0311].

To apply, please submit an online application. The closing date is 24 April 2026. Applications will receive full consideration and only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The University’s privacy policy is available on the homepage.

City University of Hong Kong is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to the principle of diversity. Personal data provided by applicants will be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes.

