Job Title: Senior Project Manager / Senior Technical Support Engineer

Location:Hong Kong

Responsibilities:
Responsible for pre-sales and after-sales technical support for ATM and other financial self-service devices;

Formulate technical and service proposals for bidding projects, and assist the marketing team in managing and advancing sales initiatives;

Provide daily technical support and management for service agents;

Develop and maintain technical documentation, including spare parts lists, service manuals, and related materials;

Collect and analyze service data, and formulate improvement plans based on statistical insights.

Requirements:
Bachelor’s degree or above, major in Computer Science, Electronics Engineering or Mechanical Engineering. Familiar with the working principle about the mechanism, electron and optics;

Minimum 3 years working experience in technical support or project management, with good performance record. Experience in ATM industry or similar banking equipment industry is preferred;

Ability to communicate well in English is required and ability to speak Mandarin will be a plus;

Knowledge on computer hardware, office applications such as Microsoft Work, Excel, Outlook, Powerpoint;

Self motivated, passionate, and must be a fast learner. Outgoing & proactive personality, strong teamwork spirit & good interpersonal communication skills.

崗位職責:‌

負責以ATM為主的金融自助設備的售前、售後技術支持;

負責投標的技術及服務方案的制定,協助營銷團隊進行銷售項目的管理和推進;

負責服務代理的日常技術支持及管理;

負責備件清單、服務手冊等各種技術文檔的編寫和管理;

負責各種服務數據的收集和統計,並制定相應的改良方案。

‌任職要求:‌

本科及以上學歷,電腦科學、電子工程或機械工程專業。熟悉機械、電子等工作原理;

至少3年技術支援或專案管理工作經驗,業績良好。有ATM產業或類似銀行設備產業經驗者優先;

英語溝通能力良好,會國語優先;

熟悉電腦硬體及辦公室軟體,如Microsoft Word、Excel、Outlook、PowerPoint;

自我激勵,充滿熱情,學習能力強。個性外向積極,具有良好的團隊合作精神和人際溝通能力。

Full-time,Permanent

(REF: A3/SAP/ITD/2/NET)

Location: Sheung Wan

Roles & responsibilities:

Provide software development services including program design, coding, testing, program modules debugging and resolving of system logic difficulties;
identify, test and correct problems in computer system and update documentation to reflect all changes of the computer system;
provide consulting and problem solving services to users in resolving business and operation problems;
provide round the clock crash maintenance and technical support for production systems;
develop training materials and conduct training courses to users under the supervision of superiors; and
advise user on course of action on system operation, enhancements and workaround.

The ideal candidate should have/be:

a recognized degree in Information Technology (IT) or equivalent;
3 years of relevant post-qualification experience in IT system development, support and maintenance services;
well-proven working experience in various IT system development with practical programming skills;
good knowledge of software and database technologies with relevant solutions on various operating system platforms;
good knowledge in the development of healthcare information systems particularly in gerontechnology and eHealth solutions is advantageous;
preferably experience in web-based system development on Microsoft ASP.NET, C#, SQL Server, HTML5 and JavaScript as well as mobile application or/and AI-based development; and
able to work independently under pressure and deal with various community services users in good interpersonal skills.

(Please specify in the resume or application form the relevant qualifications, working experience and technical knowledge you have attained in detail.)

Compensation & employment terms:

The successful candidate will initially be offered a 3-year contract with a remuneration package which will be commensurate with his/her background and experience. The continuation of employment and employment terms thereafter will be subject to mutual agreement. Apart from contributions to the MPF Scheme, other benefits include paid annual leave, medical services, a dental scheme and training sponsorships.

Application:

Please send your resume or a completed application form [F601(n)] with indication of your current and expected salaries to the Head of Human Resources Division, Tung Wah Group of Hospitals at 4/F., Wong Fung Ling Memorial Building, 12 Po Yan Street, Hong Kong or email to hrdps@tungwah.org.hk by 23 April 2026. Application forms are obtainable in person or can be downloaded from http://www.tungwah.org.hk. The reference code should be marked both in the letter and on the envelope/email. For proper delivery of your mail items, please ensure your mail items bear sufficient postage with return address before posting. Underpaid mail items will not be accepted by Tung Wah. In accordance with the Tung Wah’s personal data policy, personal data provided by the applicants will be used strictly for recruitment purpose only. Applicants not invited to attend an interview within 3 months after the deadline may assume that their applications are unsuccessful.

WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITIES EMPLOYER

The eMPF Platform Company Limited is a wholly owned subsidiary of the Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Authority (MPFA) responsible for building and operating the eMPF Platform (eMPF). The eMPF is a major public utility which aims to standardize, streamline and automate the existing mandatory provident fund (MPF) scheme administration processes. It is the most significant reform of the MPF System since its introduction in December 2000.

For background and details of the eMPF Platform, please go to our website https://www.empf.org.hk

We are looking for high calibre and passionate individuals to join us to undertake this transformation initiative that is leading the MPF ecosystem to a new era and is creating a positive impact on the working population of Hong Kong.

The Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Authority (MPFA) invites full-time undergraduates to join our 2026 Summer Internship Programme (Programme). The Programme aims to provide tertiary students with opportunities to gain real-life work experience and a better understanding of the MPF System and the MPFA. The paid full-time internship will run for two months, from 15 June 2026 to 14 August 2026.

We are offering summer internship opportunities in the following business units:

Corporate Services Division - Finance Department;

Corporate Services Division - Human Resources Department;

Information Technology Division - Digital Strategy and Solutions Department;

Member Protection and Services Division;

Policy and Regulation Division; and

Supervision Division

The Job

The main responsibilities of summer interns include:
Support the operations of the designated business unit;

Assist in digitalization initiatives or other short-term projects;

Provide administrative and clerical support;

Conduct research and data analysis; and

Perform record management

The Person

Full-time undergraduates, preferably majoring in Business Administration / Accountancy / Finance / Economics / Human Resources Management / Actuarial Science / Computer Science / Social Sciences / Law / Public Administration / Sustainability;

Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua);

Proficient in PC applications, including MS Word, Excel and PowerPoint;

Familiarity with video editing or programming is an advantage;

Strong research and analytical skills, with proficiency in using relevant tools such as Bloomberg and Power BI;

A team player with good interpersonal skills; and

Interest in a career in the public sector.

Key Dates

Application deadline: 22 April 2026

Interview selection: Mid-May 2026

Appointment: By May 2026

Internship Period: 15 June to 14 August 2026

To Apply

Interested candidates are invited to apply via our online application system ( link). The closing date for application is 22 April 2026 . Applicants who have not been invited for interview by the end of June 2026 may assume that their applications have been unsuccessful and their application forms will not be retained for more than two years. For enquiries, please send an email to [email redacted, apply via Company website].

The information provided will be kept confidential and only be used for those purposes relating to your application. Please visit our website for the details of the MPFA’s Personal Information Collection Statement at https://www.mpfa.org.hk/en/mpfa/joining-mpfa/job-vacancies/personal-information-collection-statement. The MPFA and its subsidiary are equal opportunities employers and welcome applications from all qualified candidates.

