Role Overview
We are seeking a Purchaser – Greater China to support and manage sourcing activities for Mainland China health supplements (nutraceuticals) and related materials.
This role places strong emphasis on hands-on sourcing, data analysis and materials management, working closely with suppliers, factories and internal teams to ensure stable supply, quality compliance and cost effectiveness.
Candidates who are practical, resilient, and familiar with Mainland China working culture will be highly regarded.

Key Responsibilities – Purchasing & Supply Chain
Act as a Purchaser within the Purchasing Department;
Source health supplements and related materials primarily from Mainland China;
Handle price negotiation, payment terms, purchase orders (PO), shipping documents, order follow-up and payment arrangements;
Analyze supplier quotations, cost structures and purchasing data to support procurement decisions;
Coordinate with suppliers and production teams on production schedules and delivery arrangements;
Liaise with factories for quality monitoring, compliance requirements and production follow-up;
Work closely with warehouse and internal departments on materials planning, inventory control and replenishment;
Maintain stable product supply and consistent quality standards;
Perform cost comparison, procurement analysis and reporting;
Travel to Mainland China when required for supplier meetings, factory visits and market assessment.

Advanced Responsibilities (for experienced candidates)

Candidates with solid sourcing or China-related experience may be considered for a more senior purchasing role, with extended responsibilities including:
Direct negotiation and relationship management with Mainland China suppliers;
Sourcing, evaluating and auditing new OEM / health supplement suppliers;
Conducting on-site factory audits, quality verification and capacity assessment;
Improving supply chain stability and cost efficiency;
Supporting strategic sourcing decisions through data-driven analysis.

Key Focus Areas
✅ Mainland China health supplements / nutraceuticals sourcing
✅ OEM and private-label supply chain management
✅ Data analysis, cost breakdown and supplier comparison
✅ Materials management, replenishment planning and inventory optimization
✅ Supplier quality assurance and compliance monitoring

What We Value

Rather than purely industry background, strong intuition, common sense, resilience and analytical thinking are critical success factors for this role.
The position may involve hands-on follow-up and coordination with Mainland China counterparts.

Requirements
Strong interest and knowledge in health supplements, nutrition, food or related health products (essential);
Excellent command of spoken and written Mandarin, with native Cantonese required;
3–4 years or above experience in purchasing, sourcing, trading, supply chain or China-related roles;
Prior working experience in Mainland China is a strong advantage;
Solid numerical sense with proficiency in Excel for data analysis and reporting;
Able to handle multiple tasks and work under pressure;
Self-motivated, resilient, responsible and willing to learn;
Strong team player with good communication skills;
Disciplined, punctual and detail-oriented.

Highly Preferred Qualifications
Holder of Chinese Medicine-related certificate
Holder of Nutritionist / Nutrition-related professional certification
Educational or professional background in health, nutrition, food science or related disciplines

We offer 5-day work, Free lunch, Monthly incentive, 12- 17 days annual leave, Birthday leave, 10 days paternity leave, Employee purchase discount, Medical insurance and Annual body check to the above position.

